# {{project_name}}

<!-- stacks:fill: one or two sentences on what this project does and who it's for -->

A JSON API on Hono in `backend/` and a React single-page app on Vite in `frontend/`. The frontend calls the API through a TanStack Query client generated from the API's OpenAPI document. Each part has its own README with its own commands.

## Getting started

Requires Bun, Node and make.

```sh
make install
make api-client   # backend/openapi.json, its copy in frontend/, the generated client
make dev          # the API on :3000, the app on :4173 proxying /api to the API
```

Open http://localhost:4173. To change ports, copy `.env.example` to `.env`, or export `PORT_API` and `PORT_WEB` in the shell, which wins.

